   "tender": {
    "id": "709595450 (DInfoCom0240)",
    "title": "Army Digital Discovery and Exploitation Call Off",
    "description": "The Provision of Army Digital Governance & Exploitation Support for a scalable Digital Change and Exploitation team of a core team of 4-5 roles, provided as a service, would be able to continue extant initiatives and provide accountable outputs. \r\nThere is insufficient knowledge, skills, expertise (KSE) and capacity within the Business as Usual IX Digital Governance Team to deliver these activities.  Therefore, to enable this significant and ongoing Digital Transformation, IX-Digital requires contracted support to deliver against desired following outcomes:\r\n\r\nDrive Change.  Continue to modernise through supporting data and user migration in base services overseas and from DII(S) to MODNET (Secret); support sites and Army organisations through the Windows 10 upgrades and the management of the technical refresh/user behaviour changes and upskilling needs.  Aid the adoption and improvement of Defence Gateway capabilities to allow more robust Whole Force and cross-boundary collaboration, including changes and improvements resulting from Defence Connect Army Expansion, IdAM and DGW365. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nUnlock Opportunities.  Unlock constrained capabilities through controls and risk mitigation.  Undertake discovery initiatives and develop and deliver guidance materials, advice, engagement and upskilling to key cohorts to unlock potential and to aid organisations in their own adoption and digital transformation journeys. \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nRealise Benefits.  Drive momentum and counter inertia, harnessing and exploiting broader complimentary initiatives to enable increased efficiency, effectiveness and Knowledge and Information access across the whole force and deliver greater flexibility and agility to organisations.",
